  "question": {
    "text": "If the perpendicular bisector of the line segment joining the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-intercept equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, then a value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is;"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>15</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Mid point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PQ</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br />And slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PQ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br />So equation of perpendicular bisector of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PQ</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br />It&#39;s <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> intercept <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. So, this equation must&nbsp;satisfy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>"
  }
